=== sync-count.log: one sync per layer, N per token (G5 boundary; rework: MEASURED) ===
date: Sun Nov 8 01:00 UTC 2026

Rework (BLOCKER-7E-1): boundary_syncs/drain_syncs are real in-code counters
incremented at the actual hipStreamSynchronize call sites (reset per layer,
before ensure(), so first-layer growth drains count toward that layer). The
LayerGuard is armed only while an exception is unwinding, so the normal path
performs exactly ONE sync per layer call.

== measurement 1: in-code counters (GFX1150_STREAM_TRACE=1) ==

First (cold) layer of a fresh process - growth drains are real and counted:
  [7E-trace] seq=6 projections=7 ... boundary_syncs=1 drain_syncs=22 ...
    (workspace/weight-slot growth on a fresh process; documented, one-off)

Warm layers (the steady state; every layer after growth):
  [7E-trace] seq=1 projections=7 copy_ms=0.0820 kern_ms=0.0857 overlap_ms=0.0354
              overlap_pct_of_kern=41.28 boundary_syncs=1 drain_syncs=0 hipHostRegister=0 slab_fallback=7
  [7E-trace] seq=1 ... boundary_syncs=1 drain_syncs=0 ...
  [7E-trace] seq=1 ... boundary_syncs=1 drain_syncs=0 ...
  (every warm layer measures boundary_syncs=1 and drain_syncs=0)

Asserted by tests/test_stream_topology.py::test_7e_trace_reports_one_sync_per_layer:
every layer call must measure exactly one boundary sync, and the last (warm)
layer must measure (boundary_syncs=1, drain_syncs=0).

== measurement 2: rocprofv3 --hip-trace (API level) ==

$ rocprofv3 --hip-trace -o /tmp/rocprof_out/p7e -- python3 qaqc-probes/sync_count_probe.py
$ python3 qaqc-probes/sync_count_analyze.py /tmp/rocprof_out/p7e_results.db
total hipStreamSynchronize records: 23
syncs per call cluster (index 0 = cold; rest warm): [21, 1, 1]

The probe performs three consecutive forward_layer_cached calls separated by
300ms sleeps: the cold call (cluster 0) contains the growth drains plus its
boundary sync; each warm call (clusters 1, 2) performs EXACTLY ONE
hipStreamSynchronize — the layer boundary. This is the API-level confirmation
of the auditor's original 26-record finding (which showed the pre-rework warm
call performing 3 syncs: unconditional guard drain x2 + boundary).

== source enumeration (attention.hip) ==

$ grep -n "hipStreamSynchronize" src/kernels/attention.hip
(AttentionWorkspace::ensure growth drains — legacy host wrapper, realloc only)
(DeviceLayerWorkspace::drain() — growth/exception-guard/destructor paths, counted in drain_syncs)
(exactly one steady-state call: hipStreamSynchronize(ws.copy_stream) after the final D2H,
 counted in boundary_syncs — one per launch_forward_layer_cached_fp16 call)

== boundary semantics ==

A token through an N-layer model therefore performs N boundary syncs. A
one-sync/token claim is NOT made: the Python forward_layer_cached API returns
host hidden states per layer (rework brief section 6; ledger row 15 stays
NOT YET). Growth/exception drains are separate, counted, and documented.
